From a56cc57c75917686fb65fb8f722d851e68e76cd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:57:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] llama: keep the previous graph results when the scheduler
 re-reserves

llama-server calls llama_set_sampler() for every request, so
sched_reserve() runs at the start of every request (36 ms in the server
log of the GPU layout). It destroyed the previous graph results and the
next decode made new ones, with a new meta buffer. Every tensor of the
next graph then had a new address. The CUDA backend keys its graphs by
the first node of each split, so no verify graph of the earlier request
was found again: a server trace showed new keys for the verify splits in
each of 3 requests. In every request the first verify step ran all 49
splits directly, the second captured 48 of them and the third captured
the last one.

A previous graph result with the same node limit is now only reset, as
the other places that discard old graphs do. Its meta buffer stays, and
the same graph gets the same tensor addresses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6MCJC4HTKxvuGjKjqDuqQ
---
 src/llama-context.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
index 5fd08c423..722ccc3c3 100644
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -636,8 +636,14 @@ void llama_context::sched_reserve() {
 
     LLAMA_LOG_DEBUG("%s: max_nodes = %zu\n", __func__, max_nodes);
 
+    // Keep a previous graph result of the same size and only clear it: its tensors then stay at the same
+    // addresses, and the CUDA backend finds its graphs again by the first node of each split.
     for (auto & res : gf_res_prev) {
-        res.reset();
+        if (res && res->get_max_nodes() == (int64_t) max_nodes) {
+            res->reset();
+        } else {
+            res.reset();
+        }
     }
     gf_res_reserve.reset(new llm_graph_result(max_nodes));
     gf_res_prev_active = nullptr;
